## 4️⃣ Good Practices & Hardening  

| Aspect | Recommended Implementation |
|--------|---------------------------|
| **Secrecy** | Use `.env.development`, `.envproduktion` with `.secret` 4(x64)      |
| **JWT Expiry** | 15mn – 30mn – 1h (default). Offer refresh token in backend (`/auth/refresh`) |
| **Refresh Token Strategy** | Keep it storeable (localStorage) – set expiry 7d, rotate on every use. |
| **Logging** | Use NestJS `Log` provider. Forward to structured services (`@nestjs/swagger`). |
| **Rate‑limit** | Implement `rate-limit` middleware (`@nestjs/common` or `@nestjs/cors`). |
| **GlobalErrorHandler** | Use `@nestjs/common` `GlobalExceptionFilter` + `@nestjs/swagger` to generate Swagger JSON/PDF. |
| **CORS & Sec‑Headers** | Use `@nestjs/cors` + `swagger-jhipster` implementation. |
| **Content‑Security‑Policy (CSP)** | Define a MD5 CDN policy in HTML `<meta>` tags; it reduces XSS risk from third‑party widgets. |
| **Secure API Calls** | Enclose all network operations in `AuthService` and always verify token expiration before request. |
| **User Persistence** | After login, save "remember me" flag and store a UUID (Salting ID) in cookie. |
| **API Versioning** | Store version in URL query (`/v1/users`) and sanitize `apiFilter`. |
| **Testing** | Write unit tests for services with `@nestjs/testing`. Use `@nestjs/m_after_pipeline` for testability. |
| **Security + User Experience** | Use **Formik** with `Yup` validation scheme. Hide password field after login. |
| **Testing** | Use **Cypress** or **Playwright** to exercise: login, dashboard, logout. |
| **Database Seining** | Use `Jest` (or `Vips`) for Node tests – keep secrets out of mocks. |
| **Database** | Use PostgreSQL + Prisma or Sequelize; set `PERFORMANCE` policies; enable SSL;  |
| **Environment (Serverless)** | Set `process.env.NODE_ENV = 'test'` correctly, use `process.env` for configuration. |
| **Boost Security** | Use ` dove – set up issue security` (GitHub Security Lab) for sandbox |

